Consideration of Bid #M-14-10 for a contract between the City of Cheyenne and Naranjo
Civil Constructors, Inc., of Greeley, CO for the 17 Street Parking Lot Project (State Loan and
th
Investment Board).   Mr. Brown moved to approve in an amount not to exceed $97,017.00, seconded
by Mr. Valdez.  Mr. Spiker declared a conflict of interest (owner of business property located in the
vicinity) and vacated Council Chambers.  Upon inquiry regarding possible use of a portion of the
lot during construction, Bob Bradshaw, Special Projects Director, explained the contract is for a 30
day construction window and if any of the lot was left open for use during construction the project
could risk being delayed and it is planned to have the lot completed by the Cheyenne Frontier Days
celebration.  He stated notification through the Downtown Development Authority and the City will
be made to those individuals who utilize the parking lot advising of alternate parking areas during
construction.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body present in Council
Chambers.  Following announcement of the vote, Mr. Spiker returned to Council Chambers.
